### VS Code REST Client scratchpad. Install 'humao.rest-client', then click "Send Request".
@host = http://localhost:8000

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Readiness — 503 until the PHREEQC databases are installed
GET {{host}}/readyz

### What the API can do: databases, phases, the parameter registry
GET {{host}}/v1/catalog

### Site search (hits the live USGS service)
GET {{host}}/v1/sites?state=CO&limit=5

### Analyses at one site, with the representative sample and a readiness verdict
GET {{host}}/v1/sites/USGS-06730200/samples?start=2022-01-01&end=2024-12-31&aggregate=median

### Render the PHREEQC input without running it — check the units before you trust the answer
POST {{host}}/v1/runs/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sample": {
    "site_id": "USGS-06730200",
    "measurements": [
      {"key": "ph", "value": 7.4, "unit": "std units"},
      {"key": "ca", "value": 88, "unit": "mg/l"},
      {"key": "mg", "value": 24, "unit": "mg/l"},
      {"key": "so4", "value": 64, "unit": "mg/l"},
      {"key": "alk_caco3", "value": 250, "unit": "mg/l"},
      {"key": "fe", "value": 45, "unit": "ug/l"}
    ]
  },
  "spec": {"database": "phreeqc.dat", "saturation_phases": ["Calcite", "Dolomite", "Gypsum"]}
}

### Run it
POST {{host}}/v1/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sample": {
    "site_id": "USGS-06730200",
    "measurements": [
      {"key": "ph", "value": 7.4, "unit": "std units"},
      {"key": "ca", "value": 88, "unit": "mg/l"},
      {"key": "alk_caco3", "value": 250, "unit": "mg/l"}
    ]
  },
  "spec": {"database": "phreeqc.dat"}
}

### Rejected: file access is not permitted, even for authenticated experts
POST {{host}}/v1/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{"raw_input": "DUMP\n    -file /tmp/leak.txt\nEND\n", "spec": {"database": "phreeqc.dat"}}

### Expert input that is allowed
POST {{host}}/v1/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{"raw_input": "SOLUTION 1\n    units mg/l\n    pH 7.2\n    Ca 88\n    Alkalinity 210 as HCO3\nEND\n",
 "spec": {"database": "phreeqc.dat"}}

### Metrics
GET {{host}}/metrics
